# Definitions for the tests of scripts/eal/eal.py (scripts/tests/test-eal.sh), in the form
# `lake exe geb-defs` writes. Typable unless marked otherwise:
#   twice        λf. λx. f (f x) at T -> T
#   foldOnce     a fold into functions whose step applies its argument once
#   foldTwice    the same, applying it twice: not typable
#   iterTwice    iteration of twice
#   squareByIter iteration of adding a label to itself, the label used twice:
#                typable only with first-order data exempted
# and, compiled by the stage-0 compiler from the datatype language,
#   twoPasses    a fold at pairs of a tree and a thunk whose step reads its list of the
#                children's pairs twice, once for the trees and once for the thunks:
#                not typable, the list of thunks being contracted
#   onePass      the same fold, its step splitting the list once (unzipR)
# with their helpers sum, rawsOf, forceAll, thunksOf and unzipR.
# Definitions refer to earlier ones by position, so the compiled ones come first.
